>>
Rule 1 (output_size should be a sequence containing 3 or 5 elements when provided)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 3 ∨ v_1.len = 5
>>
Rule 2 (input tensor and indices tensor should have same dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 3 (If output_size is given, the dimension 0 of output_size must be between -2 and 2)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= if v_1.len > 0 then -2 ≤ v_1[0] ∧ v_1[0] ≤ 2
>>
Rule 4 (input and indices tensors must have the same shape.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 5 (indices tensor must have integer dtype (1-5))
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5
